2523:Run crypto-digest, worker-responsiveness and browser-store once in each exact engine. crypto-digest is a same-realm WebCrypto SHA-256 known-answer check. worker-responsiveness uses the ready-gated real Phase 2f-c module-Worker workload and the thresholds in section 5. browser-store executes the production browser store's begin/stage, blob cache, promotion, completion, head swap, close, reopen and recovery path. It does not add the inherited reference vote CAS because Phase 5c owns the first production vote store/schema.
2598:EvidenceImageDigest is a test-evidence checksum only, never a protocol ClosureDigest or registered wire domain. It is lowercase SHA-256 over UTF-8 stable JSON of the closed image: object keys recursively sorted, array order preserved and Uint8Array represented as an object with sole key bytes whose value is its integer byte array. The exact same serializer and digest routine owns every old/new/reopen/retry/recovered image checksum.
